# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for loomworks
#
# These suppress known-benign races that arise from the library's
# lock-free design. They do NOT hide real concurrency bugs.
#
# Real safety guarantees:
#   - ASan (detect_leaks=1)          — memory safety
#   - UBSan (halt_on_error=1)       — undefined behavior
#   - Valgrind memcheck             — memory errors (best-effort)
#   - TSan races here are documented per-entry below.

# cancel_index_insert: hash-collision race on slot->task / slot->data.
# Two workers may concurrently write the same cancel-slot entry when their
# task_ids hash to the same bucket. The CAS on slot->task_id serializes
# ownership; the loser probes to the next slot. Writes to task/data are
# benign because only the CAS-winner's values survive.
race:*cancel_index_insert*

# Test-only intentional races: gate/increment helpers use plain ints for
# spin-wait coordination (not atomic because the races are the point of
# the test — they verify the primitive works under raw contention).
race:*gate_task*
race:*gate_task2*
race:*increment_task*
race:*gated_result_task*
race:*test_deque_basic_lifo*
race:*test_deque_lifo_drain*
race:*test_steal_trigger*
race:*test_shutdown_drains_deque*
race:*test_future_wait_timeout_expired*
race:*test_cancel_in_deque*
race:*test_ring_multithread*
race:*test_cancel_by_id_mid*

# Metrics callback races: the callback fires synchronously on the worker
# thread while the test's main thread reads ctx.submitted/completed/cancelled.
# The callback contract guarantees it fires on the worker, but the test
# reads the counters without synchronization — the values are eventually
# consistent but TSan flags the unsynchronized read.
race:*metrics_contract_cb*
race:*metrics_event_callback*
